# A238986

Write the decimal digits of n and take the absolute differences of the digits, repeating until a single digit remains. Then sum all digits of each level of the resulting triangle. If the sum is greater than 9, repeat the entire process until result is between 0 and 9, which is a(n).

The 60 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `0`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

